Hmm wait, one more scenario — the empty message with errorMessage flag itself? `_noteQuietMessageEnd`: if `message.errorMessage != null` it prints the dim note "(truncated...)" — so the tolerated silent truncation flag is set on messages that DID produce text usually. If the empty message itself carries the errorMessage flag (silent truncation with zero content?) — the empty check passes (no text/calls), and its own flag... it IS in the window? No — it's excluded (it's `message`). So an empty-with-flag message: evidence scan of the window might find nothing → cleanEmpty → nudge. Hmm — but a silent truncation with NO content means the stream was cut before anything arrived — that's exactly a hiccup-ish truncation! Should the message's OWN truncation flag count as evidence? E6: "the tolerated silent-truncation flag (no finish_reason from the provider) [counts] as partial-context evidence". The incident: "mid-code truncation" — the truncated text WAS produced. So the flag rides the truncated (text-bearing) message → covered by the window scan. For an empty message carrying its own flag: I'd say the message's own flag signals a broken stream → treat as partial evidence too. Hmm, but strictly the ticket says "the previous assistant message carried a truncation signal". Let me include the message's own errorMessage truncation flag as evidence as well? Careful — over-triggering: EVERY tolerated-truncation-flagged empty would retry (N times) — that's the desired hiccup behavior, honestly. But it changes... hmm, wait: does an empty message with errorMessage + stop=stop exist? `_streamEndedWithoutTerminal` produces StopReason.error with a message — that's abortedOrError. The silent-truncation flag (`errorMessage != null` with stop=stop) comes from adapters when no finish_reason — let me check openai adapter quickly. Actually let me not over-engineer: I'll count the truncation signal on any AssistantMessage in the window INCLUDING the classified one if it carries the flag... n