content.thinking:
Even `cat -A` shows `[REDACTED:Sensitive Value]` — so the FILE on disk really contains the redacted text. The write tool corrupted it at write time: my original write contained `token = source.token,` — and the redaction pipeline turned `source.token` into `[REDACTED:Sensitive Value]`!! (Because "token" matches a secret-ish pattern — "token = value"!)

So the redactor targets things like `token = <value>` patterns. I must avoid literal `token = source.token` in file content passed through write/edit. Workaround: write it differently, e.g. `_source = source` with field access, or construct differently. Let me rewrite the fake class to store the source only and expose `token` via getter... but getter body also would contain `source.token` — hmm, that's `source.token` not `token = x`. The redacted pattern seems to be `token = source.token` (an assignment). Let me just store only the source and use `source.token` inline:

```dart
class _CancelAfterEmptyStreamFunction {
  _CancelAfterEmptyStreamFunction(this.turns, this.source)
    : cancelOnTurn = turns.length - 1;

  final List<List<AssistantMessageEvent>> turns;
  final CancelTokenSource source;
  final int cancelOnTurn;
  CancelToken get token => source.token;
  ...
}
```

`this.source` avoids the assignment pattern. And `token` as a getter — `=> source.token;` should be safe.

Let me rewrite that class block via python with the safe shape.

arguments.command:
python3 - <<'EOF'
p = 'test/agent/agent_loop_test.dart'
s = open(p).read()
old = """class _CancelAfterEmptyStreamFunction {
  _CancelAfterEmptyStreamFunction(this.turns, CancelTokenSource source)
    : REDACTED_SENTINEL,
      cancelOnTurn = turns.length - 1;

  final List<List<AssistantMessageEvent>> turns;
  final CancelToken token;
  final CancelTokenSource source;
  final int cancelOnTurn;"""
# the file may contain the corrupted initializer; find the class block and replace wholesale
import re
pattern = re.compile(r"class _CancelAfterEmptyStreamFunction \{.*?\n\}", re.DOTALL)
m = pattern.search(s)
assert m, "class block not found"
new_block = '''class _CancelAfterEmptyStreamFunction {
  _CancelAfterEmptyStreamFunction(this.turns, this.source)
    : cancelOnTurn = turns.length - 1;

  final List<List<AssistantMessageEvent>> turns;
  final CancelTokenSource source;
  final int cancelOnTurn;

  CancelToken get token => source.token;

  final contexts = <Context>[];

  int get calls => contexts.length;

  AssistantMessageEventStream call(
    Model model,
    Context context, {
    CancelToken? cancelToken,
  }) {
    final index = contexts.length;
    contexts.add(
      Context(
        systemPrompt: context.systemPrompt,
        messages: List.of(context.messages),
        tools: context.tools,
      ),
    );
    final stream = AssistantMessageEventStream();
    for (final event in turns.removeAt(0)) {
      stream.push(event);
    }
    stream.end();
    if (index == cancelOnTurn) source.cancel('test abort');
    return stream;
  }
}'''
s = s[:m.start()] + new_block + s[m.end():]
open(p, 'w').write(s)
print("ok")
